.TH "YAMLR-VERIFY" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBCryptographic Manifest Signature Verification\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr verify\fR command verifies the cryptographic non-repudiation signature and Semantic DNA integrity of signed Kubernetes manifests \fB[Pro]\fR.
.PP
---
.PP
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
.RS
yamlr verify [path] [flags]
.RE
.fi
---
.PP
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
The \fBverify\fR command provides a supply-chain trust anchor for GitOps and regulated enterprise environments (SOC2, HIPAA, PCI-DSS).
.PP
Yamlr embeds a cryptographic signature directly into \fBmetadata.annotations['yamlr.dev/signature']\fR. When \fByamlr verify\fR is run:
.PP
1. It canonicalizes the manifest AST on disk.
.PP
2. Extracts and verifies the cryptographic signature against the embedded or local public key.
.PP
3. Mathematically proves that the manifest has not been modified or tampered with since it was signed.
.PP
---
.PP
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
# Verify all signed manifests in the current directory
yamlr verify .

# Verify a specific signed manifest
yamlr verify deployment.yaml

# Verify in CI/CD pipeline gate (blocks merge on tampering)
yamlr verify ./manifests/prod/
.RE
.fi
---
.PP
.SH "OPTIONS & FLAGS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fBpath\fR** *(positional, optional)*:
    Path to manifest file or directory of manifests. Defaults to \fB.\fR.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--k8s-version <VERSION>\fR**:
    Target Kubernetes schema version context.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB-f, --output-file <PATH>\fR**:
    Path to write verification report (JSON).
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--exit-zero\fR**:
    Exit with code \fB0\fR even if verification fails.
.PP
---
.PP
.SH "EXIT CODES"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB0\fR** (\fBEXIT_SUCCESS\fR): Manifest signatures are cryptographically valid.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB1\fR** (\fBEXIT_VIOLATIONS\fR): Signature mismatch, manifest tampered, or unsigned.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB4\fR** (\fBEXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR\fR): File I/O failure or missing manifest.
